sections.贯穿案例：一次内部报表功能上线:
All figures are illustrative assumptions that show the arithmetic; they are not vendor quotations or any team's real person-days.

- Input: an internal reporting assistant for operations staff. It reads customer email bodies, outputs only aggregates, and does not modify records.
- Processing, split into four items (illustrative assumptions):
  Gap analysis: 32 control points at about 0.25 person-days each = 8 person-days;
  evidence production: 6 deliverables (flow map, log sample, evaluation record, policy note, permission table, review record) with one rework round = 12 person-days;
  review rounds: legal, security and business, 2 person-days each = 6 person-days;
  upkeep: one redo per quarter at 3 person-days = 12 person-days per year.
- Judging the result (example): 26 person-days for the first pass, 12 per year for upkeep.
  The decisive uncertainty is whether customer email bodies form a data category that triggers extra duties —
  if they do, evidence production and review rounds both have to be recomputed.
- What to do after a failure:
  Turn that uncertainty into two actions: confirm the data-category call with legal, confirm the processor role with the vendor;
  before the answer lands, present two cases (yes / no) instead of a fake midpoint;
  once settled, update the assumption list and the verification date, keeping the estimate traceable.

Unit rates are yours to enter: convert person-days into your own basis and then multiply.
This page gives no amounts and assumes no exchange rate, tax or discount.
